Z||000003||SLYGUY||10-08-2001||12:45 AM||||Great find Sootah.<P>Should be a great car. <BR>You never told us how it ran though. Probably have to do all the same fun stuff the rest of us had to do. For some reason the original owners stopped caring about the little things that are so easy to fix  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><BR>What do you mean about the standard driver's side rip in the seat? My interior was pristine. Perhaps because it is the holy grail of Fieros....the 88GT 5spd.<BR>Just joshin'<P>Great find and good luck with it!!<P>Sly<BR>You ne||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mach10||10-08-2001||02:59 AM||||A good wash with a decent car detergent should do it. Failing that, Mother's Clay Bar should do it. Last-ditch, use a rubbing compound that's safe for clear-coats.||||reg||6
Z||000005||Sootah||10-08-2001||08:14 AM||||Ran great. Was sitting for a bit, I could tell the owner had not even touched it for who knows how long. I was expecting a long crank followed by sputtering and all of that other I-Havent-Been-Started-in-3-months shìt, but NOTHING. Started right up and purred like a kitten. Gawd I'm happy.<P>Plans as soon as I get her home today:<BR>New Cap, Rotor, Plugs, Wires<BR>K&N filter<BR>run a bottle of fuel system cleaner through her (Reccomendations?)<BR>Oil change (synthetic)<BR>Wash the living crap out of it, folloewd by some polishing compound, another wash, and some wax.<BR>Take pics and show my beauty off to my forum buddies.<BR>Mail 1 pic off to my friend on a mission in NJ (Apt. 2 miles from former WTC) telling him the mileage, condition, and price. Should be able to hear his screams from here.<P>Hee hee, he bought an 85-86 SE in not near as good condition for $2500. BOO-YAH GRANDMA!! He's gonna blow a freakin fuse.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
